  "id": "gondhal",
  "name": "Gondhal (Marathi goddess ritual song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Gondhal is a Marathi ritual performance in which Gondhali singers invoke the goddess, above all Tulja Bhavani of Tuljapur and Renuka of Mahur, through the night at family ceremonies such as weddings, singing invocations and narrative songs. The lead singer plays the tuntuna, a one-string plucked drone, while a companion beats the sambal, a pair of drums played with sticks, and others answer on cymbals and in chorus. The gopichand card, a one-string plucked drum, stands in for the tuntuna.",
